  "grammar_points": [
    {
      "name": "〜故に (yue ni - because of)",
      "jlpt_reference": "JLPT N2",
      "explanation": {
        "en": "A literary and formal way to say \"because of\" or \"due to.\" It sounds much more elegant than the everyday から (kara) or ので (node). You will mostly find it in written Japanese, poetry, and song lyrics.\n\nHow it works:\nAttach 故に (yue ni) after a verb in past tense, a noun, or a na-adjective + な. It marks the reason or cause for what follows.\n\nExample from this song:\n愛した故に芽生えた悪の花 (aishita yue ni mebaeta aku no hana, \"Because I loved, a flower of evil bloomed\")\n\nMore examples:\n- 若さ故に (wakasa yue ni, \"because of youth\")\n- 知らなかった故に (shiranakatta yue ni, \"because I did not know\")\n- 彼女が好きだった故に (kanojo ga suki datta yue ni, \"because I liked her\")"
      },
      "conjugation_path": "愛する (aisuru) → 愛した (aishita) → 愛した故に (aishita yue ni)"
    },
    {
      "name": "〜であろう (de arou - probably is/will be)",
      "jlpt_reference": "JLPT N2",
      "explanation": {
